#-------------
T:The Thumby
T:is
T:manufactured
T:by
T:TinyCircuits
T:and is a 
T:tiny keychain
T:programable
T:mini-gameboy.
T:It can be
T:coded in 
T:MicroPython
T:and maybe
T:Aurduino.
T:It might
T:also be
T:possible in
T:C but
T:requires you
T:making a .uf2
T:file.
T:
T:The Thumby
T:boasts a 
T:RP2040
T:Dual ARM
T:Cortex-M0+
T:with up to
T:133 MHz.
T:This and
T:paired with
T:264 KB of
T:SRAM and 
T:2 MB of
T:total storage.
T:With a 
T:beautiful
T:Monochrome
T:OLED 72x40
T:pixel 
T:display.
T:Featuring a 
T:40 mAH LiPo 
T:battery 
T:cranking up
T:to 2 hours 
T:of playtime.
T:The Thumby
T:has a LOT
T:of games 
T:crafted by
T:the community
T:and some 
T:golden titles
T:like Thoom
T:or Thumbgeon.
T:Another
T:amazing
T:recent works
T:is MidiPlayer
T:which enables
T:you to play 
T:chiptune
T:songs from
T:your Thumby.
T:
T:Back to Wiki
